// A statement with no control flow of its own. When it is a call that never
// returns (front/diag/noret), the block ends there with the program's answer,
// and what follows lands in a fresh block nothing reaches. When it calls a
// function that may exit, the block is cut after it instead: the runner looks
// at the exit status between blocks, so the statements after the call never run
// once the callee has exited.
walk_plain(int id) {
  add_lowered(id);
  int nr = stmt_noreturn(id);
  walk_end(id, nr);
} return void;
